1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,500
Senate Democrats are currently debating this idea of whether to place conditions on the funding.

2
00:00:05,900 --> 00:00:12,600
One of the arguments in favor is that Congress does this for nearly every other country that it gives foreign military assistance to.

3
00:00:12,820 --> 00:00:13,900
What is your response to that?

4
00:00:13,960 --> 00:00:14,980
I think it's ridiculous.

5
00:00:15,500 --> 00:00:22,700
Our relationship with Israel is the closest national security relationship we have with any country in the world.

6
00:00:22,700 --> 00:00:33,020
And to condition, in effect, our assistance to Israel on their meeting our standards, it seems to me, is totally unnecessary.

7
00:00:33,640 --> 00:00:45,940
This is a democracy, a great ally of ours, and I do not think we need to condition the support that hopefully we'll give to Israel very soon.

8
00:00:45,940 --> 00:00:58,980
Okay, so maybe you're like, I mean, I don't care about if Israel is holding Palestinians in an apartheid regime.

9
00:00:59,100 --> 00:01:00,340
Like, I just don't care about none of that.

10
00:01:00,340 --> 00:01:10,600
Maybe you care about the fact that when America is giving all this money to Israel, they are able to do things with it that America says it cannot do for Americans.

11
00:01:10,940 --> 00:01:13,540
They have universal health care.

12
00:01:14,040 --> 00:01:16,380
They have free college.

13
00:01:17,060 --> 00:01:18,760
They have housing.

14
00:01:18,760 --> 00:01:28,740
Like, these are things that America says we don't have the power, but yet we're giving money to a country that is able to implement that to its own citizens.

15
00:01:28,920 --> 00:01:30,120
That should bother you.

